  "summary": "A three-slab coral limestone trilithon at Heketā on Tongatapu, said to have been built about 1200 CE by the 11th Tu'i Tonga, Tu'itatui. It is believed to have served as a gateway to his royal compound; a later royal study linked its lintel notches to the sun's movements.",
